{
  "_doc": "Per-weapon audio profiles (0.5, brief 17). A profile names the recorded set a weapon fires (assets/audio/weapons/<set>, built by gradlew prepareAudio), how its layers are balanced, and what its action does after each round. Firing code never chooses a sound: it posts a shot and this table decides. Gains are linear. rate is the playback rate applied to every layer of the set (1 = as recorded). tailMakeupDb lifts every recorded tail by that much before the per-weapon tail gain (the library was recorded close and dry: its decays sit about 40 dB under the report). variation: per-shot bounds for playback rate (+-) and level in dB (+-). mech: events relative to the shot in seconds, each a handling sample (assets/audio/handling). suppressed: how the same recordings are rendered through a suppressor (no separately recorded suppressed sets exist in the library - see the manifest).",
